# R23 hook: Dani at the ruins and Tamsin in the village. Drafted by hand, polished by Gemini (R23 hook), unvoiced.

~ dani_ruins
Narrator: The spirits have stopped circling the wrecked house. They stream north across the dark heather in a pale, silent current, while Dani Jenkin stands among the fallen beams, watching them go.
dani_jenkin [neutral]: They know the way. They're going to Adela. Phillip is out on the turf too, lost, with his lantern dark. They have shut her in a basket of woven branches with the others, where the light is terrible.
set wv_hook_given
set wv_started
quest wickers_vigil follow_the_spirits
-> dani_menu

~ dani_menu
* Ask what she senses out there -> dani_feel
* Ask where Phillip has gone -> dani_phillip
* Ask about the face in the storm -> dani_face
* We'll follow the dead north -> dani_go
* We should warn the village first -> dani_village

~ dani_feel
dani_jenkin [afraid]: Dry wood that has waited all year for a spark. Dozens of people shut inside the willow ribs, listening to an old song they cannot block out.
-> dani_menu

~ dani_phillip
dani_jenkin [sad]: The marsh-lights have him. They're coaxing him deeper into the mire while he calls her name. By the time he sees the hill, it will be too late.
-> dani_menu

~ dani_face
dani_jenkin [neutral]: That's the Crooked Man. He has traded his roof for the thunderhead. He'll talk to you along the heather track. Most of what he says is wicked, except the part about the fire.
-> dani_menu

~ dani_go
dani_jenkin [neutral]: Keep to the path the ghosts take. The high track across the moor is quickest, though the climb at the end feels longer than it is.
Narrator: She offers no farewell, only turns back toward the cold ash while the hound sits fast at her heel, ears pricked toward the clouds.
-> END

~ dani_village
dani_jenkin [neutral]: Tamsin has her ledger out in the square. She'll want your names down before you march. Everyone left is gathered at the Round, if you mean to say goodbye.
-> END

~ dani_again
dani_jenkin [neutral]: The last of the pale ones have passed by. It's only the dog and me in the dirt now. Hurry along, before the pitch catches.
* We're on our way -> END

~ tamsin_start
Narrator: A clerk has brought order to the end of the world. A trestle table blocks the cobbles, a patient queue curls past the well, and every face in the square is turned toward the red glare on the northern ridge.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Ah, the household our neighbours insist on leaving their latches off for. The willow giant on Rowan's Rise is alight, and our muster roll is a shambles. I am recording volunteers in triplicate. Step down to the barricade and report.
set wv_started
quest wickers_vigil follow_the_spirits
-> tamsin_menu

~ tamsin_menu
* Ask what happened here -> tamsin_what
* Ask about the wicker effigy -> tamsin_wicker
* Join the village at the barricade -> tamsin_come
* Head straight for the moor road -> tamsin_moor

~ tamsin_what
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Neighbours in hare masks seized the constable first, and the mayor has vanished. At sundown they lit a beacon on the rise, and the clouds took on a grin. I have minuted the particulars.
-> tamsin_menu

~ tamsin_wicker
tamsin_ledger [weary]: Sixty feet of woven osier, by the look of the ridge. Currently entered under Structures, Unauthorised. Once the sparks reach the thatch, I shall reclassify it under Arson.
-> tamsin_menu

~ tamsin_come
tamsin_ledger [smile]: Good. Watch your shins on the breastwork. Until noon it was a turnip cart.
move wv_square:from_travel

~ tamsin_moor
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: The north track leaves just past the Round. If you return in one piece, kindly initial the gate ledger on your way through.
-> END

~ tamsin_again
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Everyone who remains is down in the Round, if you wish to look them over before you climb the hill.
* Take us down to the Round -> tamsin_come
* Not just now -> END
